{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"practice-专项-source-f85ed9915446","kind":"practice","title":"【未上传】试题部分WORD—5年高考、3年模拟_专题十四主旨要义（可作答题）","year":"专项","region":"资料","variant":"可作答资料","instructions":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"专题十四　主旨要义"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"【5年高考】"}]}],"sections":[{"id":"section-legacy","title":"旧卷综合题型","instructions":[],"layout":"flow","groups":[{"id":"group-legacy","instructions":[],"stimulusBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A组　统一命题·新高考卷、课标卷题组"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Passage 1　　主题语境:人与自然　　词数:291　　限时:8分钟"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"　　(2021新高考适应卷,D)The average bear, it seems, is getting ever smarter. First, it turned out that at least one can use a comb. Now it appears that some can count, too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Jennifer Vonk, of Oakland University, in Michigan, and Michael Beran, from Georgia State University, set three American black bears the task of distinguishing between numerically larger and smaller groups of dots(点)on a computer screen. In return for a food reward one bear, Brutus, would touch the more heavily dotted pattern with his nose. The others, Bella and Dusty, would touch the screen with their claws(爪子)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"As the researchers report in Animal Behavior, the bears did best with patterns where the coloured dots did not move and where more of them also took up a larger coloured area. This could be explained by the bears' distinguishing the different areas of colour rather than truly counting the dots. However, the three bears managed to pick out the bigger number of dots even in pairs of patterns where fewer dots took up a larger area."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Moving patterns, where each dot followed its own path around the screen, were more of a challenge. But Brutus, at least, was not defeated. He seemed to be counting mobile dots even when the scientists tried to mislead him by moving the total coloured area of the dots at the same time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"It is not entirely surprising that bears should have a high degree of intelligence. They face a lot of challenges when trying to get food. They are, however, always alone, and so do not have the complex social systems that contribute to animal smarts. Perhaps, then, their maths skill developed because they cannot count on their friends for help."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"1.What task did the scientists set for the three bears?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A.Distinguishing different dot patterns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"B.Figuring out different colours of dots."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"C.Putting the dots into differently coloured groups."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"D.Picking out the group with a larger number of dots."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"2.For the bears, the task was easier when　　　. "}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A.the coloured dots were moving slowly"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"B.the dot patterns were regular in shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"C.the dots followed a path on the screen"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"D.more dots covered a larger coloured area"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"3.What may explain the bears' high degree of intelligence?"}]}],"sharedOptions":[],"questions":[{"id":"q-1","displayNumber":1,"sourceQuestionNumber":1,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"What task did the scientists set for the three bears?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishing different dot patterns."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Figuring out different colours of dots."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Putting the dots into differently coloured groups."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Picking out the group with a larger number of dots."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["C"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"f85ed9915446dce36bd25b55510efd0a979f5a3c658e142665ade088da2789f7","relativePath":"题型/【未上传】试题部分WORD—5年高考、3年模拟_专题十四主旨要义.docx","sha256":"f85ed9915446dce36bd25b55510efd0a979f5a3c658e142665ade088da2789f7","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.96}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"9ef4d7a0ebecf4298d47d1e23fbc55f409724f9a8f6dfe8d94bfe25fa7a59658","answerVariantFingerprint":"80505fd5c0ef6d00be017c584deff225c00956ccf5d6a2f8e1937dde281a8781"}},{"id":"q-2","displayNumber":2,"sourceQuestionNumber":2,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"For the bears, the task was easier when . A."}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"the coloured dots were moving slowly"}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"the dot patterns were regular in shape"}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"the dots followed a path on the screen"}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"more dots covered a larger coloured area"}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"f85ed9915446dce36bd25b55510efd0a979f5a3c658e142665ade088da2789f7","relativePath":"题型/【未上传】试题部分WORD—5年高考、3年模拟_专题十四主旨要义.docx","sha256":"f85ed9915446dce36bd25b55510efd0a979f5a3c658e142665ade088da2789f7","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.96}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"f0b0564b53f4087ffab42196642d685a67dc1e1efe81afb20e45b4c2956b10be","answerVariantFingerprint":"0be754b6230dd24619ec6d1402806db8d8864ccbad5dfb855c3785115d6d621d"}},{"id":"q-3","displayNumber":3,"sourceQuestionNumber":3,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"What may explain the bears' high degree of intelligence?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"They learn skills from other animals."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"They face life challenges on their own."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"They feed on a diverse range of food."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"They have complex social networks."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["A"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"f85ed9915446dce36bd25b55510efd0a979f5a3c658e142665ade088da2789f7","relativePath":"题型/【未上传】试题部分WORD—5年高考、3年模拟_专题十四主旨要义.docx","sha256":"f85ed9915446dce36bd25b55510efd0a979f5a3c658e142665ade088da278